# Normalise to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Prettier's default is `endOfLine: "lf"`, so a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true hands contributors CRLF files that git then reports as
# unmodified, and `pnpm lint` fails on files nobody changed. Pinning the
# checkout to LF makes the lint result depend on the content rather than on
# which machine produced it.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's binary detection, so sprites and archives in
# public/assets are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
